\par I specifically challenge the validity of sensitive documents generated by AI in that particular system, declare why this is faulty especially with subjective data
\par In a probabilistic system like ValueCare's generative assistant, using large language models (LLMs) to construct sensitive psychiatric or clinical documents is fundamentally faulty. Subjective data\emdash 
such as a patient's self-reported trauma, emotional nuance, or a clinician's subtle qualitative impressions\emdash cannot be reliably mapped using statistical token probabilities.
\par When a system treats fluent text generation as the authoritative record of a human mind, it introduces structural defects that compromise clinical safety and data integrity.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang8192\langfe1033\langnp8192\insrsid9708344\charrsid9708344 Why Probabilistic AI Fails with Subjective Data
